Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3.  The algebraic anomaly equation and its integration", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ced98ea9-bd99-46cb-b7ae-543308c9df94"],

Cell["\<\
We write the anomaly equation as in theorem 4.12 and solve it using the idea \
from Theorem 4.15.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000535458859007*^9, 4.000535482847781*^9}, {
  4.000772873018888*^9, 
  4.000772927234291*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5963868a-3d3b-4a07-acb1-\
f1091f0efbd3"],

Cell["\<\
DD  = s0^6 - s4^6;           (* vanishes exactly at the conifold *)
vv  = s4^3/s0^3;             (* v^2 = 3^6 z_A *)\
\>", "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.000772931085203*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[545]:=",ExpressionUUID->"454f0a19-a5dc-47e9-b70e-2978879429e0"],

Cell["the vector fields as operators", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"77c2a93e-a97e-4fc4-8637-d058fcc165e4"],

Cell["\<\
Rop[i_][f_] := Cancel[Together[td[f] /. RV[i]]];
R0op[f_]    := Cancel[Together[td[f] /. R0]];\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[547]:=",ExpressionUUID->"bac09d5b-178d-41db-980d-d68fed1721df"],

Cell["\<\

\\cal G^chi := I^chi s0^(2 chi) G^(chi),   and more generally
A[chi,n] := I^chi s0^(2 chi) (3/Gzz)^n G^(chi)_n . (covariant derivative)

R_0 becomes the covariant derivative (lemma 4.10):
R_0 A[chi,n] = A[chi,n+1]     (verified in checks.wl)
because R_0 = 3 Gzz^-1 d/dz_A,  R_0(s0) = -(3/2) s0 Kz/Gzz  and
R_0(Gzz) = 3 Gammazz.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0005355054447927`*^9, 4.00053551435747*^9}, {
  4.000535571524169*^9, 4.0005355816084213`*^9}, {4.000535632888321*^9, 
  4.000535677941552*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"08dd983e-0c84-4b12-9c5c-\
f842a395efb5"],

Cell["\<\
G01seed = (1/2) (Czzz (Szz + (1/2) Deltaz^2) + 144/24 Kz
                 + (1/12 PP/zA - 7/(3 zA)  + 1/8 (PP - 1)/zA));   (* G^(0)_1 *)
Gm12seed = (1/2) Deltazz;                                          (* \
G^(-1)_2 *)

A[0, 1]  = Cancel[Together[(3/Gzz) G01seed]];
A[-1, 2] = Cancel[Together[I^(-1) s0^(-2) (3/Gzz)^2 Gm12seed]];
A[c_, n_] := (A[c, n] = R0op[A[c, n - 1]]) /; (c == 0 && n > 1) || (c == -1 \
&& n > 2);
A[c_, n_] := (A[c, n] = R0op[A[c, n - 1]]) /; c >= 1 && n >= 1;
(* A[chi,0] = \\cal G_chi is filled in by SolveChiAlg below *)\
\>", "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000535843895421*^9, 4.0005358500748653`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[549]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3988da3e-50fb-40c3-a621-f412b11da875"],

Cell["", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000535598058919*^9, 
  4.000535612010673*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"727ba532-473c-40b4-816c-\
6d90b1233929"],

Cell["\<\
The next cell is exactly the two last equations from Thm 4.12 and Thm 1.1. \
The first two equations are taken care in function Partials[chi_], where they \
are used implicit in the computation.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0005358798417473`*^9, 4.0005359252245293`*^9}, {
  4.000535956593178*^9, 4.000535983946842*^9}, {4.000772990474318*^9, 
  4.000772994226288*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5cd2a54d-104d-47c0-928e-\
6fe001daec67"],

Cell["\<\
RHS4[chi_] := Cancel[Together[
   3^-8 (Sum[A[j, 1] A[chi - 2 - j, 1], {j, 0, chi - 2}] + A[chi - 2, 2])]];
RHS7[chi_] := Cancel[Together[-3^-8 A[chi - 1, 1]]];\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[557]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ea175f25-b1a5-4751-afec-98541c69823c"],

Cell["\<\
The function Partials[chi_] compute the derivatives from the information we \
have from the anomaly equation for G^chi. See Thm 4.15.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000535709332199*^9, 4.00053577429488*^9}, {
  4.000535985073435*^9, 4.00053599023209*^9}, {4.000773003314404*^9, 
  4.000773003884981*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e096ca0a-7bc5-4e4d-a276-\
163596489601"],

Cell["\<\
Partials[chi_] := Module[{r4, r7, r5, d1, d2, d3, d5, d6, d7, d8, c31},
  r4 = RHS4[chi];  r7 = RHS7[chi];
  d6 = Cancel[Together[s5 r4/(27 s0^4 DD)]];    (* R4 = (27 s0^4 DD/s5) d/ds6 \
*)
  d7 = r7;                                       (* R7 = d/ds7            *)
  r5 = Cancel[Together[-Rop[3][r4]]];            (* [R3,R4] = -R5         *)
  d1 = Cancel[Together[-(1/2) Rop[3][r5]]];      (* [R3,R5] = -2 R6 = -2 \
d/ds1 *)
  d8 = Cancel[Together[-Rop[3][r7]]];            (* [R3,R7] = -R8 = -d/ds8 *)
  d2 = Cancel[Together[(s5 r5 + (135 s0^8 - 54 s0^2 s4^6 + s3) d1)/(27 s0^4 \
DD)]];   (* from R5 *)
  d5 = Cancel[Together[-(s6 d6 + s7 d7)/s5]];    (* from R1 Ghat = 0      *)
  c31 = (135 s0^6 s5 + s2 s5 - 135 s0^8 s6 + 54 s0^2 s4^6 s6 - s3 s6)/(27 \
s0^4 DD);
  d3 = Cancel[Together[-(c31 d1 + s6 d2 + s7 d8)/s5]];             (* from R3 \
Ghat = 0 *)
  <|s1 -> d1, s2 -> d2, s3 -> d3, s5 -> d5, s6 -> d6, s7 -> d7, s8 -> d8|>];\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[559]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a6d22337-53e3-45b4-9381-c304a4b6783a"],

Cell["\<\
Direct integration. First we create a functions for antiderivative and after \
we reconstruct G^chi from its derivatives.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000535997875916*^9, 
  4.0005360767260427`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7be40988-6ebc-48d1-81ca-\
4a518b2ce497"],

Cell["\<\
antiD[f_, v_] := Module[{g, n, d, cl},
  g = Together[f]; n = Numerator[g]; d = Denominator[g];
  If[! FreeQ[d, v],
     Message[antiD::nonpoly, v]; Return[Integrate[f, v]]];
  cl = CoefficientList[Expand[n], v];
  Cancel[Together[Sum[cl[[k]] v^k/(k d), {k, 1, Length[cl]}]]]];\
\>", "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000536011996747*^9, 4.000536012546834*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[560]:=",ExpressionUUID->"8c37521d-c6ee-4bcb-8027-063973cf2e70"],

Cell["", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  4.000536027841918*^9},ExpressionUUID->"14508dd3-06ae-42dc-b416-\
f3dfed546e37"],

Cell["\<\
Reconstruct[chi_] := Module[{P = Partials[chi], g = 0, h, rem, chk},
  Do[h = Cancel[Together[P[v] - D[g, v]]];
     g = Cancel[Together[g + antiD[h, v]]],
     {v, {s7, s6, s8, s1, s2, s3}}];
  g];\
\>", "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0005360844598513`*^9, 4.000536096145534*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[561]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a5e72d73-81f1-4cbb-b223-c2baf301daa8"],

Cell["We construct the ambiguity as in section 5.", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000536108525819*^9, 
  4.00053611717402*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"46388ea8-1812-4a08-a6c1-\
c38237f48a5c"],

Cell["\<\

AmbKs[chi_] := Range[Mod[chi, 2], 3 chi, 2];
Ambiguity[chi_, sym_: amb] := Total[
   Table[sym[k] s0^(2 chi) vv^k (1 - vv^2)^((chi - k)/2), {k, AmbKs[chi]}]];\
\>", "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000536128043571*^9, 4.000536128528173*^9}, {
  4.000536165084607*^9, 4.000536195047557*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[562]:=",ExpressionUUID->"4951c303-c855-4eff-8906-dc1fa92c51de"]
}, Open  ]],

